Yes. I went through the repo as an **archive audit**, using the scored manifest plus the high-signal files and representative files from each family. The repository currently contains roughly four different projects entangled together: **RoboBladez gameplay**, **AI-character persistence/evolution**, **speculative consciousness/quantum experiments**, and **unrelated CODI/Digital Tom experiments**. The manifest makes that mixture obvious: `quantum.txt`, `q2.txt`, Gen-3/4/5 evolution papers, multiple Architect prompts, BattleStar Boris variants, `actually good blades`, RoboBladez thesis/overview, CODI modules, HSQER robot experiments, and duplicates across several directory trees.

My conclusion is: **there is an excellent game hidden in here, but probably only ~15–20% of the conceptual material belongs in the actual build.**

